// @trap
// @hint redundant type annotation: `k` is inferred as `i32` — remove it to lean on inference
// `u as! i32` over a type parameter pinned at `f64` traps on a fraction, as `x as! i32` over
// an `f64` does, rather than truncating it (D2791).
function k<T>(u: T): i32 { u as! i32 }
print(k<f64>(1.5))
print(-1)
